INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(7460660, 1182955, 18677, '<td valign="top">Great composition and colors!</td>', 'Great composition and colors!', '2016-06-18 22:37:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460671, 1182964, 18677, '<td valign="top">Great focus and sharpness. Good lighting. The background seems a bit too distracting and unnatural, although it''s nice that the colors match their shirts. I think a larger aperture / shallower DOF would''ve helped a lot here, to soften the background without taking away the good colors.</td>', 'Great focus and sharpness. Good lighting. The background seems a bit too distracting and unnatural, although it''s nice that the colors match their shirts. I think a larger aperture / shallower DOF would''ve helped a lot here, to soften the background without taking away the good colors.', '2016-06-19 01:04:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460672, 1182942, 18677, '<td valign="top">The lighting on the hand seems a little harsh, but this definitely is one of the better entries in this challenge. Perfect amount of background blur! Enough that their faces don''t distract too much from the main subject, but not so much that you can''t see them well enough. Well done.</td>', 'The lighting on the hand seems a little harsh, but this definitely is one of the better entries in this challenge. Perfect amount of background blur! Enough that their faces don''t distract too much from the main subject, but not so much that you can''t see them well enough. Well done.', '2016-06-19 01:12:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460673, 1182983, 18677, '<td valign="top">One of the better entries in this challenge, especially in a technical sense. Good lighting &amp; focus, appropriate DOF, black background helps to emphasize the bright colors in the subject(s). If I have to critique something here, it''d be that it doesn''t have much of a "wow" factor, and the black thing(s) behind or between them seems out of place and a little distracting. Otherwise it''s a good image.</td>', 'One of the better entries in this challenge, especially in a technical sense. Good lighting & focus, appropriate DOF, black background helps to emphasize the bright colors in the subject(s). If I have to critique something here, it''d be that it doesn''t have much of a "wow" factor, and the black thing(s) behind or between them seems out of place and a little distracting. Otherwise it''s a good image.', '2016-06-19 01:24:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460674, 1182943, 18677, '<td valign="top">Nice colors, good focus and sharpness. The main problem here is the lighting. The subjects are shadowed and underexposed. It''s a good photo, but some additional light (from a fill flash or maybe a reflector) could''ve made it a lot better.</td>', 'Nice colors, good focus and sharpness. The main problem here is the lighting. The subjects are shadowed and underexposed. It''s a good photo, but some additional light (from a fill flash or maybe a reflector) could''ve made it a lot better.', '2016-06-19 01:29:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460676, 1183010, 18677, '<td valign="top">I think you might''ve dialed up the sharpness a little too much, but it''s a good photo. Good decision to use a wide DOF here. The wide dynamic range is impressive, especially with the clouds. A lot of distracting elements in the foreground and background. Without those, this would''ve been an awesome photo.</td>', 'I think you might''ve dialed up the sharpness a little too much, but it''s a good photo. Good decision to use a wide DOF here. The wide dynamic range is impressive, especially with the clouds. A lot of distracting elements in the foreground and background. Without those, this would''ve been an awesome photo.', '2016-06-19 01:59:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460677, 1182891, 18677, '<td valign="top">Nice photo. The main technical issues are that it''s not very sharp and the lighting is a bit harsh. Probably not much you could''ve done about the lighting from that distance, although a remote flash or maybe a reflector would''ve helped. The lack of sharpness might just be a limitation of your lens/camera, so I can''t take off points for that, but it might also be because your focus was just a little bit too far in front of the subjects'' faces. Also, the area near the bottom of his foot looks odd, like you tried to clone something out, and the top of her hair looks blurry, like you tried to artificially blur the background. Sounds like I just listed a lot of things wrong with it, but all of those are fairly minor and can be easily corrected. Overall it''s a good photo that meets the challenge very well.</td>', 'Nice photo. The main technical issues are that it''s not very sharp and the lighting is a bit harsh. Probably not much you could''ve done about the lighting from that distance, although a remote flash or maybe a reflector would''ve helped. The lack of sharpness might just be a limitation of your lens/camera, so I can''t take off points for that, but it might also be because your focus was just a little bit too far in front of the subjects'' faces. Also, the area near the bottom of his foot looks odd, like you tried to clone something out, and the top of her hair looks blurry, like you tried to artificially blur the background. Sounds like I just listed a lot of things wrong with it, but all of those are fairly minor and can be easily corrected. Overall it''s a good photo that meets the challenge very well.', '2016-06-19 02:11:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460678, 1182996, 18677, '<td valign="top">Good colors, focus, sharpness, and composition. Also good timing with the wave. I only see one problem with this photo, and unfortunately it''s a big one: the lighting. The subjects are very dark, but not dark enough to be silhouettes. The relatively bright water draws the eye away from them. This could''ve been a wonderful photo if you had another source of light shining toward them, such as a remote flash.</td>', 'Good colors, focus, sharpness, and composition. Also good timing with the wave. I only see one problem with this photo, and unfortunately it''s a big one: the lighting. The subjects are very dark, but not dark enough to be silhouettes. The relatively bright water draws the eye away from them. This could''ve been a wonderful photo if you had another source of light shining toward them, such as a remote flash.', '2016-06-19 02:21:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460679, 1183011, 18677, '<td valign="top">This could''ve been an awesome photo if it was only the two children in the foreground and the grass, without the other people or the distracting and unattractive building/house behind them. Your use of black &amp; white and grain helped save it a little (I''m sure this version looks much better than the original), but I just can''t get over the harsh background. The lighting is a bit harsh too (looks like it was shot during the middle of the day), which could be improved by shooting closer to sunset or on cloudy days.</td>', 'This could''ve been an awesome photo if it was only the two children in the foreground and the grass, without the other people or the distracting and unattractive building/house behind them. Your use of black & white and grain helped save it a little (I''m sure this version looks much better than the original), but I just can''t get over the harsh background. The lighting is a bit harsh too (looks like it was shot during the middle of the day), which could be improved by shooting closer to sunset or on cloudy days.', '2016-06-19 02:31:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460680, 1182985, 18677, '<td valign="top">Great photo, but I think it would''ve been better without the saturated bandannas. They jump out so much that they distract from the best parts of this image, which are the dog''s expression, the good composition, and the excellent natural framing.</td>', 'Great photo, but I think it would''ve been better without the saturated bandannas. They jump out so much that they distract from the best parts of this image, which are the dog''s expression, the good composition, and the excellent natural framing.', '2016-06-19 02:42:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460681, 1182941, 18677, '<td valign="top">I don''t like that his buckles are in focus and everything else isn''t. Would''ve been so much better if his eyes were in focus instead. But everything else about this photo is good.</td>', 'I don''t like that his buckles are in focus and everything else isn''t. Would''ve been so much better if his eyes were in focus instead. But everything else about this photo is good.', '2016-06-19 02:47:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460682, 1182709, 18677, '<td valign="top">Great photo. I love the colors. Good focus and lighting, appropriate DOF. I think it meets the challenge well enough, although some might disagree.</td>', 'Great photo. I love the colors. Good focus and lighting, appropriate DOF. I think it meets the challenge well enough, although some might disagree.', '2016-06-19 02:49:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460683, 1182979, 18677, '<td valign="top">Nice colors and composition. The main subjects seem a bit underexposed. Because you have a relatively bright background, a fill flash would''ve helped a lot. Also, the coloring on the left side of the background looks strange. Otherwise it''s a nice shot.</td>', 'Nice colors and composition. The main subjects seem a bit underexposed. Because you have a relatively bright background, a fill flash would''ve helped a lot. Also, the coloring on the left side of the background looks strange. Otherwise it''s a nice shot.', '2016-06-19 02:49:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460684, 1182973, 18677, '<td valign="top">Good idea. Nice colors. Main problem is that it''s overexposed. It''s difficult to get the exposure right with white subjects. In this case, it would''ve worked better to adjust the exposure compensation toward the negative side, then lighten up the water in post-processing. Shooting in RAW format also would help preserve some of the details on the extreme white/black ends.</td>', 'Good idea. Nice colors. Main problem is that it''s overexposed. It''s difficult to get the exposure right with white subjects. In this case, it would''ve worked better to adjust the exposure compensation toward the negative side, then lighten up the water in post-processing. Shooting in RAW format also would help preserve some of the details on the extreme white/black ends.', '2016-06-19 02:50:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460685, 1182962, 18677, '<td valign="top">The focus is good, but the background is very distracting. A larger aperture with more background blur would''ve helped a lot here. It also might''ve been better from a different angle.</td>', 'The focus is good, but the background is very distracting. A larger aperture with more background blur would''ve helped a lot here. It also might''ve been better from a different angle.', '2016-06-19 02:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7460726, 1183009, 182653, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition in this photo, the idea behind it is nice.<br/> <br/>What I really dislike is the post processing. The colours don''t fit with the mood of the image and in my opinion the image is way too gloomy and glowy. I think if you work on the colours and turn down on that glow effect this will be a great image.</td>', 'I really like the composition in this photo, the idea behind it is nice. What I really dislike is the post processing. The colours don''t fit with the mood of the image and in my opinion the image is way too gloomy and glowy. I think if you work on the colours and turn down on that glow effect this will be a great image.', '2016-06-19 17:11:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(7461252, 1182970, 175381, '<td valign="top">I love it. The B/W composition tell a story that we want to participate. I give 9 for the great work</td>', 'I love it. The B/W composition tell a story that we want to participate. I give 9 for the great work', '2016-06-22 13:28:52.000000', NULL, 1),
